  "pdf": "ads5423.pdf",
  "pages": "p.1 (features: 14-bit 80 MSPS, 5 V analog, 3.3 V CMOS outputs), p.2 (recommended operating conditions: AVDD 4.75-5.25 V, DRVDD 3.0-3.6 V, 30-80 MSPS), p.4 (digital outputs VOH/VOL, DMID = DRVDD/2), p.5 (timing: tDR CLK rising to DRY falling 4.7 ns max, DRY rises tDR + tCLKH, latency 3 cycles, data updated with CLK rising / DRY falling), p.6 (pin assignments), p.19 (digital outputs: D13..D0, DRY pin 52, OVR pin 32, two's complement)",
  "notModeled": [
    "analog input and reference (the result is always the 0 V code 0x0000)",
    "pipeline latency of 3 clock cycles (the code is constant)",
    "OVR (over-range) is modeled as an extra data bit that is always 0 (a 0 V input is never out of range): bus data is OVR, D13..D0 with read pattern \"0R{14}\"",
    "DRY is modeled as the inverted CLK (falls tDR after CLK rising, rises tDR + tCLKH later); its own delay and the data delay share tOut = 4.7 ns (tDR max)",
    "pin names: pins 6 and 12 are printed CLK and AIN with an overline (complement inputs); written CLK# and AIN#",
    "CLK/CLK# are a differential (AVDD-referenced) clock input; only CLK is the clock pin; sample rate limits 30-80 MSPS",
    "C1/C2 reference bypass pins and DMID (DRVDD/2 output) are analog"
  ],
